{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/362516-can-uratha-be-possesed-by-spirits","id":362516,"title":"Can Uratha be possesed by spirits?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-01-07T09:15:21-08:00","id":362516,"title":"Can Uratha be possesed by spirits?","content":"One of my players were not on the last game, and we come to agreement his PC was &quot;killed&quot; by Bale Hounds pack. But player want to return to game later on, so we think about nice twist on that. I asked him if he would want to infiltrate the PCs pack for Maeljins and he agree as player. But his character would not do this. So he is thinking that maybe his Cathalith is possessed by spirit putted there by Bale Hounds to work for Great Sins. Question is simple: <b>Can Uratha - being half-spirits themselves - been possessed by one?</b> Better, if the character would not be suspecting this. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-07T09:24:03-08:00","id":362539,"title":"","content":"Not sure about possession, but they sure as heck can be influenced. In 1e Philadelphia, violence-spirits are contributing to the clashes between young werewolf gangs and hunters by urging hostility and bloodlust.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">-: <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations\" target=\"_blank\">First Tongue Translation Requests</a></b> :-</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1874-sikla-alkis","name":"Sikla Alkis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1874_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-07T10:02:47-08:00","id":362584,"title":"","content":"As per Predators, werewolves can be Urged and Possessed but not Claimed. Next question? :-)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-07T10:10:32-08:00","id":362591,"title":"","content":"Would other members of the pack &quot;feel&quot; Urged or Possessed werewolf? And were in <b>Predators</b> there is this mention?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-07T10:27:22-08:00","id":362620,"title":"","content":"Generally you need to boot out the existing spirit-part of a werewolf to allow for Claimed, which is why Idigam making Empty Wolves are so terrifying.<br /> <br /> As for whether other pack members can sense the spirit Urging or possessing, I am so far into 2e mindset now that I can't remember whether you could in 1e.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-07T10:53:04-08:00","id":362688,"title":"","content":"I always wondered if that was what happened to the guy from Hunting Ground: Rockies who used a drug cocktail to stymie his First Change, thinking it was a psychotic break. He was taken advantage of by a spirit of lost possibilities, which is probably one of the worst things to happen.<br /> <br /> With the corrupting presence of Wounds and the Maeljin, it would be interesting if there was a sort of Wounded Werewolf they could make that didn't have to be Bale Hounds but were more vulnerable to the manipulations of them and other Wound-spirits.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-07T12:32:01-08:00","id":362805,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/362516-can-uratha-be-possesed-by-spirits?p=362620#post362620\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Generally you need to boot out the existing spirit-part of a werewolf to allow for Claimed, which is why Idigam making Empty Wolves are so terrifying.<br /> <br /> As for whether other pack members can sense the spirit Urging or possessing, I am so far into 2e mindset now that I can't remember whether you could in 1e.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I'm pretty sure they could, given the right gifts and abilities.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">-: <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations\" target=\"_blank\">First Tongue Translation Requests</a></b> :-</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1874-sikla-alkis","name":"Sikla Alkis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1874_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-07T13:05:23-08:00","id":362827,"title":"","content":"Werewolves can't, barring exceptional circumstances, detect spirits possessing or urging people. That would dilute the purpose of the Ridden as enemies you can't see until it's too late.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}